WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:01.580
Hey it's Kamala Harris.

00:00:01.580 --> 00:00:03.399
She's a rising star in the democratic party.

00:00:03.399 --> 00:00:05.980
Almost an Obama-like hype around her.

00:00:05.980 --> 00:00:09.060
Possibly the next President of the United
States!

00:00:09.060 --> 00:00:12.300
Last week Senator Kamala Harris finally made
it official.

00:00:12.300 --> 00:00:15.280
I am running for President of the United States.

00:00:17.240 --> 00:00:20.520
The California Democrat is trying to position
herself as a reformer

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:23.880
who works tirelessly to correct the abuses
of the criminal justice system.

00:00:23.880 --> 00:00:28.440
But the senator has one big problem: her long record as a law and order prosecutor.

00:00:28.440 --> 00:00:31.080
Harris' new memoir, The Truths We Hold,

00:00:31.080 --> 00:00:34.210
makes no mention of her past as an old school
drug warrior,

00:00:34.210 --> 00:00:37.500
a defender of dirty prosecutors and a political
opportunist

00:00:37.500 --> 00:00:40.140
who has made life more dangerous for sex workers.

00:00:40.140 --> 00:00:44.300
Harris doesn't apologize for her previous
stances, even those she now disavows.

00:00:44.300 --> 00:00:50.160
Instead she's decided to try and convince
voters she's always been a progressive prosecutor.

00:00:50.160 --> 00:00:54.300
How do you reconcile your contradictory past
with what you claim to support today?

00:00:54.309 --> 00:00:56.070
I've been consistent my whole career.

00:00:56.070 --> 00:01:01.060
Here are some of the stories the Senator is
hoping you'll forget in the run up to 2020.

00:01:01.060 --> 00:01:03.040
Harris' political rise has been propelled

00:01:03.040 --> 00:01:07.440
by a years long, high profile campaign against
alleged sex traffickers.

00:01:07.440 --> 00:01:11.160
What she's actually done is throw women in
jail for having consensual sex

00:01:11.160 --> 00:01:14.840
while trampling on the rule of law to advance
her own political ambitions.

00:01:14.840 --> 00:01:19.540
Ignoring the pleas of sex workers and human
rights advocates for over a decade,

00:01:19.540 --> 00:01:23.940
she's fought against campaigns to decriminalize
consensual adult prostitution in California.

00:01:23.940 --> 00:01:26.420
As Attorney General she created a statewide
program

00:01:26.420 --> 00:01:30.040
to get truckers to report suspected sex workers
to police.

00:01:30.040 --> 00:01:34.920
These policies didn't stop traffickers, but
they did land plenty of sex workers behind bars.

00:01:34.920 --> 00:01:37.740
One of the greatest offenders is backpage.com.

00:01:37.740 --> 00:01:40.580
Harris fought to destroy backpage.com,

00:01:40.580 --> 00:01:44.420
a classified site that sex workers used to
find and screen their clients.

00:01:44.420 --> 00:01:49.120
Even though she publicly admitted that the
sites founders, Michael Lacy and James Larkin,

00:01:49.120 --> 00:01:52.740
were protected from prosecution under federal
free speech laws.

00:01:52.740 --> 00:01:55.320
But tonight, a groundbreaking arrest.

00:01:55.320 --> 00:02:00.620
But a month before election day in her Senate
race, Harris went ahead and had them arrested anyway,

00:02:00.620 --> 00:02:03.320
parading them before the cameras on pimping
charges

00:02:03.320 --> 00:02:05.820
which were then promptly dismissed by a judge.

00:02:05.820 --> 00:02:08.180
When Harris got to Congress she kept up her
crusade,

00:02:08.180 --> 00:02:11.880
becoming a big proponent of the 2018 law known
as SESTA/FOSTA.

00:02:11.880 --> 00:02:19.420
One cannot cowardly sit behind a computer
committing their crime, quite the contrary.

00:02:19.420 --> 00:02:23.200
The result was that many sex workers had no
choice but to return to the streets

00:02:23.200 --> 00:02:26.520
where soliciting clients is considerably more
dangerous.

00:02:26.520 --> 00:02:28.220
It's cause you don't know who's gonna pick
you up.

00:02:30.640 --> 00:02:35.819
Meanwhile Harris declined to intervene in
a real underage sex trafficking scandal

00:02:35.820 --> 00:02:40.440
that involved dozens of police and other local
authorities in the bay area.

00:02:40.440 --> 00:02:42.660
America has a deep and dark history

00:02:42.660 --> 00:02:47.000
of people using the power of the prosecutor
as an instrument of injustice.

00:02:47.000 --> 00:02:49.800
I knew this history well, of innocent men
framed,

00:02:49.800 --> 00:02:53.560
of prosecutors hiding information that would
exonerate defendants.

00:02:53.560 --> 00:02:59.660
Yes and as California's top cop, Harris contributed
to that history repeatedly.

00:02:59.660 --> 00:03:02.360
By going to bat on behalf of dirty prosecutors.

00:03:02.360 --> 00:03:04.380
Her office appealed the dismissal of a case

00:03:04.380 --> 00:03:08.000
in which a prosecutor had fabricated a confession
to secure a conviction.

00:03:08.000 --> 00:03:12.420
And fought an appeal in a case where a prosecutor
had lied to the jury during trial.

00:03:12.420 --> 00:03:14.760
In 2015 Harris tried to stop the removal

00:03:14.760 --> 00:03:17.800
of the Orange County District Attorney's Office
from a murder trial

00:03:17.800 --> 00:03:21.420
after it repeatedly failed to turn over evidence
to the defense.

00:03:21.420 --> 00:03:26.900
Her office even tried to keep a man in jail
who had been wrongfully incarcerated for 13 years

00:03:26.900 --> 00:03:29.480
after a judge ruled that he had proven himself
innocent

00:03:29.480 --> 00:03:32.700
just because the man hadn't delivered that
proof quite fast enough.

00:03:32.700 --> 00:03:37.920
And as San Francisco DA Harris hid known misconduct
by a crime lab technician

00:03:37.920 --> 00:03:40.260
who admitted to deliberately tainting evidence.

00:03:40.260 --> 00:03:44.720
Prosecutors working under you know about the
concerns about that lab,

00:03:44.720 --> 00:03:46.440
which is what the judge alleged.

00:03:46.440 --> 00:03:49.320
-in my office did not know about it, at least
said they did not know about it.

00:03:49.320 --> 00:03:53.460
The debacle has since led tot he dismissal
of hundreds of criminal cases.

00:03:54.380 --> 00:03:58.840
Something else it's passed time we've done
is dismantle the failed war on drugs

00:03:58.840 --> 00:04:00.840
starting with legalizing marijuana.

00:04:00.840 --> 00:04:06.120
Your opponent Ron Gold has said that he is
for the legalization of marijuana recreationally

00:04:06.120 --> 00:04:07.500
your thoughts on that?

00:04:09.680 --> 00:04:12.720
Uhm, I, that he's entitled to his opinion.

00:04:12.720 --> 00:04:17.880
Harris is a former drug warrior who is now
fashioning herself as pro legalization.

00:04:17.880 --> 00:04:21.020
That's a positive shift, but not a reason
to rewrite the past

00:04:21.020 --> 00:04:23.420
or ignore the patterns it reveals in her judgement.

00:04:23.420 --> 00:04:28.120
For years after the cultural tide had turned
in favor of criminal justice reforms

00:04:28.129 --> 00:04:30.699
Harris continued to support lock-em-up policies

00:04:30.700 --> 00:04:32.540
that disproportionately hurt minorities.

00:04:32.540 --> 00:04:37.960
As California Attorney General Harris opposed
marijuana legalization as late as 2014,

00:04:37.960 --> 00:04:42.100
promoted civil asset forfeiture without a
conviction as a way to fight drug rings,

00:04:42.100 --> 00:04:45.360
and sought to more aggressively police prescription
drug use.

00:04:45.360 --> 00:04:49.779
In her new book, Harris reveals that her drug
warrior mentality hasn't changed

00:04:49.779 --> 00:04:51.710
it's just that her emphasis has shifted.

00:04:51.710 --> 00:04:54.410
We also need to reinstate the DA's authority

00:04:54.410 --> 00:04:58.349
to go after the major pharmaceutical manufacturers
and distributors

00:04:58.349 --> 00:05:01.550
and we need to invest resources and law enforcement
efforts

00:05:01.550 --> 00:05:04.580
to cut off the supply of fentanyl from China.

00:05:04.580 --> 00:05:12.820
Let's believe in a more perfect union, without
mass incarceration of African American men.

00:05:12.820 --> 00:05:17.720
We put more people in prison than any country
on earth for no good reason.

00:05:17.720 --> 00:05:20.800
Yes we do, and once these people were in prison

00:05:20.800 --> 00:05:23.580
Harris saw to it that they have a hell of a time getting out.

00:05:23.580 --> 00:05:27.939
I absolutely feel that there should be severe
and serious consequence for violent crime

00:05:27.940 --> 00:05:32.760
which is why I prosecuted those cases and
will always seek the highest sentence.

00:05:32.760 --> 00:05:36.320
As a prosecutor in law enforcement I have
a huge stick

00:05:36.320 --> 00:05:42.000
so I decided I was going to start prosecuting parents
for truancy.

00:05:42.000 --> 00:05:43.700
Before her recent about-face,

00:05:43.700 --> 00:05:50.340
Harris chose not to endorse proposed sentencing
reforms on the California ballot in 2012 and 2014.

00:05:50.340 --> 00:05:54.140
And she defended the constitutionality of
cash bail until 2016.

00:05:54.149 --> 00:05:58.629
Harris' office also fought an order to reduce
California's prison population

00:05:58.629 --> 00:06:03.160
after the Supreme Court determined that the
conditions amounted to cruel and usual punishment.

00:06:03.160 --> 00:06:06.200
Although she later claimed to be 'shocked'
by what they had done,

00:06:06.200 --> 00:06:10.080
Harris' attorneys argued that non violent
offenders should stay behind bars

00:06:10.080 --> 00:06:12.780
because the state needed the cheap labor they
provide.

00:06:12.780 --> 00:06:18.280
We are part of a longer story and we are responsible
for how our chapter gets written.

00:06:18.280 --> 00:06:21.140
As she blazes her path to the White House
in 2020,

00:06:21.140 --> 00:06:25.820
Kamala Harris is trying to rewrite her last
chapter, but her record remains.

00:06:25.820 --> 00:06:31.440
Our children and our grandchildren will ask
at that inflection moment, where were you?

00:06:31.440 --> 00:06:35.940
And what did you do in service of your family,
your neighborhood,

00:06:35.940 --> 00:06:37.440
your community and your country?

